<section class="home-guidance" aria-labelledby="home-guidance-title">
  <div class="home-guidance-inner">
    <header class="home-guidance-heading">
      <h2 id="home-guidance-title">Instructing Dr Qureshi</h2>
      <p>A straightforward route from your first enquiry to a psychiatric expert report. Each instruction begins with an availability and conflict check, and Dr Qureshi's opinion remains independent of the party instructing him.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="home-guidance-cards">
      <article class="home-guidance-card">
        <h3>Discuss your instruction</h3>
        <p>Send a brief outline of the case and any deadline. Once availability and the scope of the opinion are agreed, fees and timescales can be confirmed and a letter of instruction provided.</p>
        <p class="home-guidance-card-detail">Medical records are transferred securely once an appropriate method has been agreed.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="home-guidance-card">
        <h3>Arrange an assessment</h3>
        <p>A psychiatric assessment can take place at the Glasgow office, at an agreed venue elsewhere in Scotland, or remotely by secure video link where clinically appropriate.</p>
        <p class="home-guidance-card-detail">The arrangements depend on the individual circumstances and clinical requirements of the case.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="home-guidance-card">
        <h3>Receive the report</h3>
        <p>Reports are typically completed within two to four weeks of the assessment, with the reporting deadline agreed when the instruction is accepted. Urgent instructions can be considered.</p>
        <p class="home-guidance-card-detail">Supplementary and joint reports, and attendance at proof, are available where required.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a class="home-guidance-link" href="/instructions">More about instructing Dr Qureshi <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

